**Drawing required (no figure supplied):** draw a large, almost spherical eyeball cut lengthways, with the cornea bulging at the front, and label the following:

- **sclera** (tough white outer coat) and **cornea** (transparent front part of the sclera);
- **choroid** (dark, pigmented, with blood vessels) and **retina** (inner light-sensitive layer containing rods and cones);
- **conjunctiva** (thin membrane over the front);
- **iris** with the **pupil** (central opening), in front of the lens;
- **lens** (biconvex, transparent), held by **suspensory ligaments** attached to the **ciliary body (ciliary muscle)**;
- **aqueous humour** (watery, between cornea and lens) and **vitreous humour** (jelly-like, behind the lens);
- **yellow spot (fovea)** on the retina, where vision is sharpest, and the **blind spot** where the **optic nerve** leaves the eye.

Give a title and use ruled, non-crossing label lines.
